# JetonBro mandatory Cursor operating rules

Cursor must read this entire file before planning, editing, running commands, or answering any implementation request in this repository.

After every accepted change, Cursor must update this file when the change affects architecture, invariants, state transitions, accounting, permissions, commands, deployment, or the current implementation status.

Cursor must never silently weaken, bypass, delete, or contradict a rule in this file. If a request conflicts with a rule, stop and explain the conflict before editing.

## Product boundary

JetonBro is a virtual-jeton ledger for games played physically at a table.

Physical cards, card dealing, card values, player decisions, and winner determination happen offline.

The dealer is authoritative for physical gameplay. The application is authoritative for jeton accounting.

The application is responsible only for:

- player balances;
- bets and locked commitments;
- Blackjack boxes;
- Poker blinds and pots;
- recording player actions that affect jetons;
- simple turn indication;
- dealer-controlled phase/street progression;
- dealer-declared outcomes;
- payout;
- Dealer/blind rotation;
- ledger persistence.

Do not implement:

- digital cards as gameplay;
- hand evaluation;
- automatic winner determination;
- game strategy;
- card simulations;
- autonomous casino gameplay;
- visual redesign during protocol fixes.

Every feature must answer: “Is this necessary to replace physical jetons?” If not, it is outside scope.

Physical money, dealing, shuffling, randomness, and payment processing remain outside the application. Blackjack and Texas Hold’em are separate domain modules. Zilch remains coming later. Poker must never be folded into the Blackjack rules engine.

Optional Card Assist already exists as display-only rank records of physical cards. It must never evaluate a hand, choose a winner, advance a street, settle a pot, or block play. Do not expand it. Do not add a digital deck.

## Mandatory invariants

1. The server is authoritative for every balance and phase.
2. Every balance mutation creates an immutable ledger entry.
3. Every value-changing command is transactional and idempotent.
4. Ordinary bets and Insurance are separate locked-value accounts.
5. Normal box settlement never settles Insurance.
6. Insurance settlement never settles a normal box.
7. A round cannot complete while any box or Insurance bet remains unresolved.
8. A Player sees only their own boxes and balance.
9. A Player sees all their own open boxes together.
10. The permanent Player bottom area always shows their available value and jetons in every phase.
11. The Bank sees all active boxes.
12. The Bank phase label stays in a compact rail near the top. The Dealer primary phase action is anchored at the bottom.
13. Physical cards, real money, dealing, shuffling, suits, decks, and card randomness remain outside the application. Optional rank records may be stored as assistance only; they never replace the physical table and never block play.

## Blackjack phase sequence

`TABLE_SETUP -> BETTING -> PLAYING -> PAYOUT -> ROUND_COMPLETE -> BETTING`

No backward transitions and no phase skipping.

Insurance is a Bank-triggered window during PLAYING, not a phase. It is settled independently during PAYOUT.

## Texas Hold’em phase sequence

`POKER_SETUP -> PRE_FLOP -> FLOP -> TURN -> RIVER -> SHOWDOWN -> HAND_COMPLETE -> PRE_FLOP`

The Table Owner advances physical-card streets only after the current betting round is complete. Blinds post automatically once per hand. If one Player remains, the pot is awarded immediately without Showdown: the current actor and amount to call are cleared, the winner is recorded, and `HAND COMPLETE + TO CALL + WAITING` is impossible. If every remaining Player is All-In, the Owner still deals remaining streets, then Showdown. Next hand rotates the Dealer button once and posts blinds once. Physical cards stay offline; there is no shuffling, dealing, deck, or automatic hand evaluation. Optional community and hole-card records are display-only and never advance a street or settle a pot.

## Texas Hold’em roles and control matrix

These roles stay distinct. The rotating Dealer/Button is never Owner chrome.

- Table Owner (`isOwner`): manages the table and advances physical-card streets.
- Poker Dealer/Button (`seat.isDealer`): rotating playing seat; posts blinds and acts normally; does not receive Owner controls.
- Current Actor: the only Player who may Fold / Check or Call / Bet or Raise / All-In. CALL stays directly available when chips are owed. BET/RAISE opens a local composer; jeton taps and pot drops add to the staged amount and do not move the ledger or the turn until CONFIRM BET / CONFIRM RAISE. Duplicate confirmation is idempotent. The rotating Dealer/Button is never Owner chrome.
- Other Players: see the hand, pot, street, and whose turn it is; cannot act.
- Folded / All-In Players: remain visible with status and the wallet; receive no betting controls or tray.

Lower layout on every playable screen: Owner street controls sit in the phase-action area (zone 3), visually separated from actor actions above the tray. Then a fixed Player wallet (AVAILABLE on the right, shared jeton tray, signed-in Player only, safe-area padding). Hide controls the user cannot use; show a disabled street button only to explain that the street is not yet matched. Clients follow snapshot/SSE; `pokerControls()` is the UI acceptance contract.

| Phase | Owner (not acting) | Owner (also actor) | Current actor (not owner) | Other Players | Folded / All-In |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `POKER_SETUP` | START HAND; SEAT ORDER / + PLAYER / GIVE JETONS / SWITCH GAME in the table menu | — | — | Same felt + wallet | — |
| `PRE_FLOP` | DEAL FLOP visible disabled until matched | DEAL FLOP disabled + actor actions + tray | Actor actions + tray; no DEAL | Same felt; whose turn; wallet; no actions | Seat status + wallet; no actions/tray |
| `FLOP` | DEAL TURN disabled until matched, then enabled | Same + actor set if it is their turn | Same as PRE_FLOP | Same | Same |
| `TURN` | DEAL RIVER disabled until matched, then enabled | Same | Same | Same | Same |
| `RIVER` | SHOWDOWN disabled until matched, then enabled | Same | Same | Same | Same |
| `SHOWDOWN` | AWARD POT | No actor actions | No actor actions | Pots/results + wallet | Status + wallet |
| `HAND_COMPLETE` | NEXT HAND; countdown / jetons / switch in the table menu | No actor actions | Wallet + result | Wallet + result | Wallet + result |

## Accounting

- Unit: millijetons (`bigint`, 1000 = 1 jeton). Floating-point arithmetic is not used for balances.
- AVAILABLE is `TableMember.availableMillis`.
- LOCKED_BET is `BettingBox.lockedBetMillis`.
- LOCKED_INSURANCE is `InsuranceBet.amountMillis` until Insurance is settled.
- LOCKED_POKER is `PokerParticipant.lockedMillis` until the hand is awarded. Poker wagers move `AVAILABLE → LOCKED_POKER` and never debit or credit `BANK_VIRTUAL_RESERVE`. Side pots follow all-in contribution levels. Split pots divide equally; millijeton remainder is assigned left of the dealer button.
- BANK_VIRTUAL_RESERVE is unlimited and not stored as a balance. In Open Bank it is the source of minted table jetons and payout profit, and the sink of lost ordinary and Insurance stakes.
- Limited Bank stores table-specific `BANK_AVAILABLE` and `BANK_LOCKED_EXPOSURE` in millijetons. Initial funding is `BANK_VIRTUAL_RESERVE → BANK_AVAILABLE` once. Before a Player stake is accepted, the Bank reserves maximum configured box profit exposure (`1.5×` for 3:2, `1.2×` for 6:5). Insurance reserves `2×` Insurance stake independently. Settlement consumes or releases that reserved exposure in the same transaction as the Player ledger. The Player is credited exactly once by the existing `BET_*` / `BLACKJACK_RETURN` / `INSURANCE_*` entry. `BANK_PAYOUT` and `BANK_STAKE_TAKE` are Bank-side legs (`playerId` null), never a second Player credit. Insufficient coverage rejects the Player action without debiting them.
- Commands that change value require an idempotency key and write at least one ledger entry in the same transaction.
- Ordinary payouts: win profit 1× / return 2×; push profit 0 / return 1×; loss return 0; Blackjack 3:2 profit 1.5× / return 2.5×; Blackjack 6:5 profit 1.2× / return 2.2×.
- Insurance 2:1: profit 2× Insurance stake / return 3× Insurance stake. Settled independently of the box.

## Permissions

- Owner: create table, invite, add a local Player by name without email, add/remove players before a round, assign Bank/Dealer, rename the table, distribute jetons, save table, close table and transport remaining AVAILABLE to `PLAYER_POCKET`, permanently delete an unused empty draft, or use Owner-only `END & DELETE` on an abandoned active table as a recoverable termination (not a physical ledger wipe). Dealer reassignment does not transfer ownership. An Owner who is not the Bank still receives the table menu on the Player surface.
- Bank/Dealer: open betting, deal cards, Insurance window, payout phase, settle boxes, settle Insurance, start next round. Optionally enter/correct ranks on any Player box and the Dealer hand during PLAYING. During PAYOUT the table owner may use `DEALER WON` to settle every currently unresolved active Player box as `LOST` in one transaction; already-settled boxes stay unchanged and Insurance is never settled by this command. May toggle Open/Limited Bank during unstaked BETTING. The Open/Limited toggle is shown only in the table menu on the Bank BETTING surface. Players never see it. May change Card Assist during TABLE_SETUP or unstaked BETTING. A Dealer who is not the Owner cannot rename, assign Dealer, remove Players, switch games, save, or close.
- Player: own boxes only; bet/retract during BETTING; Double/Split during PLAYING; Insurance only while the window is open. Optionally enter/correct ranks on their own selected box during PLAYING. Never edit another Player’s box or the Dealer hand. In Texas Hold’em only the current actor may Fold/Check/Call/Bet/Raise/All-in. The rotating Dealer/Button is a seated Player and does not inherit Table Owner street or table-management controls.
- Table Owner: may switch games during TABLE_SETUP, unstaked BETTING, ROUND_COMPLETE, POKER_SETUP, or HAND_COMPLETE. Locked Bet, Insurance, Bank exposure, or LOCKED_POKER blocks switching with `Finish or clear the current hand before switching games`. Switching preserves the table, memberships, AVAILABLE, pockets, owner, invitations/QR, and seat order. Limited Bank buckets freeze in place during Poker and restore unchanged on return to Blackjack.

## Design architecture

- `tabletop` is the default skin (`ACTIVE_SKIN_ID = "tabletop"` in `src/ui/skins/registry.ts`). `classic` remains registered as the rollback skin; switching back is a one-line registry change.
- Game/domain logic must not import skin components or CSS.
- Skins must not contain permissions, accounting, phase rules, or payout calculations.
- Build shared semantic slots first, then render those slots through the active skin.
- A future skin must be replaceable without changing domain tests.
- Do not create per-skin copies of pages or game logic.

Recommended skin boundary:

```text
src/ui/core/                 semantic screen composition
src/ui/skins/classic/        Classic components, tokens and styles (rollback skin)
src/ui/skins/tabletop/       Tabletop components and tabletop.css (default skin)
src/ui/skins/registry.ts     typed skin selection
```

Tabletop skin (`src/ui/skins/tabletop/`) is a complete `JetonBroSkin` and is isolated from Classic:

- It imports only `./tabletop.css` (from `index.ts`). It must never import Classic components, helpers or CSS. Classic CSS must not load into the client bundle while Tabletop is active: `registry.ts` imports Classic via `./classic/skin` (components only); Classic stylesheets live in `./classic/styles` and are not imported when `ACTIVE_SKIN_ID` is `tabletop`. Every Tabletop rule is scoped under `.tabletop-skin` / `[data-skin="tabletop"]`. `isolation.test.ts` enforces this and that the registry activates `tabletop`.
- It reuses only `src/ui/core/*` semantics (`blackjackDealerControls`, `blackjackPlayerControls`, `blackjackOwnerMenu`, `playerBoxSlots`, `joinQrDataUrl`, `addChipToAmount`), `@/application/queries/poker-controls` (`pokerControls` stays the Poker UI acceptance contract) and `@/domain/jetons/chips` (local `chipsFromMillis`). It sends commands only through the existing `onCommand`. It contains no permissions, accounting, phase rules or payout calculations.
- Visual authority order for Tabletop: (1) original approved PNGs under `design/reference/classic/approved/`; (2) product phase/control/role contracts; (3) Tabletop implementation; (4) `jetonbro-player-bank-insurance.html` only as a secondary token colour reference; (5) historical/implementation screenshots are never design authority. Compressed JPG copies under `design/reference/tabletop/approved/` are not primary references.
- The PNGs control visual anatomy, shapes, typography, palette, density and component appearance. The product specification controls real data, legal actions, command labels, role privacy, phase progression, bottom Dealer controls, Player tray, invitations and accounting.
- Composition: full-height phone table (`100vw` max `480px`, `100dvh`, no page scroll). Compact header (menu + role/balance). Designed felt surface with a structural curved gold rail. Bottom rail holds Dealer phase dock and/or Player tray. Dealer Blackjack uses the approved dense ledger/row composition for real Players and boxes only—never kidney plaques, never fabricated empty seats. Player boxes use the approved box silhouette with layered jetons. Poker seats sit around the felt with the pot at the centre, D/SB/BB markers, a pulsing (reduced-motion: static) actor outline, and Owner street control in the rail separated from actor actions above the tray.
- Rejected presentation that must not return: CSS diamond-hatch wallpaper felt, 2px decorative ellipse rail, dashed-circle chips, kidney/spatial Dealer plaques, `data-arc` / `data-dealer-positions` as visual contracts, giant page-heading table names, generic flat web cards as finished controls.
- Canonical Blackjack dock labels, Player labels and `data-table-board` board ids remain the product contract. Presentation markup may be replaced completely without changing game logic, commands, handlers, accounting, permissions or snapshots.
- Not implemented in Tabletop (optional, display-only, deferred): Card Assist rank entry sheets, outcome celebration overlays and the welcome shimmer. Rollback to Classic restores them.

Do not preserve rejected visual anatomy merely because tests assert it. Behavioural tests protect commands, legal actions, balances, roles, overflow and accessibility. Tests must not prescribe rejected class names, kidney spots, or Classic-only selectors.

Classic CSS has exclusive ownership boundaries:

- `tokens.css`: design tokens only
- `layouts.css`: responsive geometry only (not Blackjack composition)
- `table.css`: shared phone felt + Poker objects
- `blackjack-classic.css`: canonical Blackjack Dealer and Player presentation
- `home.css`: Home and Create Table only
- `invite.css`: shared invite/sheet owner used by Create Table and Phase 0
- `board.css`: shared live-table shell (header, phase rail, docks) — not Blackjack box/ledger anatomy

A selector must not style unrelated surfaces. Remove obsolete rules instead of layering new overrides. Do not use `!important` to resolve architectural cascade conflicts.

There must be one canonical visible component for Home, Create Table, Phase 0, Blackjack Dealer, Blackjack Player, Poker Dealer and Poker Player. Adapter components may remain only when a documented caller requires them. No two route/component paths may independently implement the same visible screen.

Authenticated Home uses the approved Saved Tables composition. Each card prioritises the table name and a concise game/state indicator. Resume/Open and owner actions remain available but must not make the card look like an administration record. Player count, Owner and Dealer metadata may live in the overflow/details surface and are not required on the card face. `CREATE TABLE` remains the primary Home action.

Normal `CLOSE TABLE` follows the existing safe-boundary accounting rules.

An Owner may also choose `DELETE ALL MY TABLES` for every table they own (draft or active). This is Owner-only, confirmed by typing `DELETE ALL`, and runs as one idempotent server operation: each owned table is terminated/archived and hidden, invitations revoked, ledger/history kept, no settlement or fabricated results, and other Owners’ tables are untouched.

An Owner may also choose `END & DELETE` for an abandoned active table. This is a distinct destructive operation with a confirmation sheet naming the table and warning that the current hand/round will be abandoned.

`END & DELETE`:

- is Owner-only;
- is available from the Home overflow menu and swipe reveal;
- revokes invitations;
- hides the table from all active user surfaces;
- marks the table terminated/archived using the existing recoverable deletion model;
- does not physically delete ledger, round or accounting history;
- does not attempt normal settlement or fabricate winners;
- cannot affect another table;
- is rejected for non-Owners;
- must be idempotent.

This exception exists for abandoned/test tables and does not change normal round completion, settlement or `CLOSE TABLE` behaviour.

Visual reconstruction must not rename or relocate commands in a way that changes behaviour. The canonical Blackjack dock remains:

- Phase 0: `START BETTING` | `ADD PLAYER`
- Betting: `DEAL CARDS` | `ADD PLAYER`
- Playing: `ENTER PAYOUT` | `OPEN INSURANCE`
- Insurance open: `ENTER PAYOUT` | `CLOSE INSURANCE`
- Payout unresolved: result controls + disabled `START BETTING`
- Payout resolved: `START BETTING`

Player:

- Betting: `PLACE BET` / `RETRACT` / `ADD BOX`
- Playing: `2×` / `SPLIT` / `INSURANCE` according to legal flags
- Payout: results only
- Jeton tray and AVAILABLE remain at the bottom.

## Deployment

- One Next.js app, one PostgreSQL database.
- In-process SSE is single-instance only. Railway must run exactly one application instance.
- `GET /api/health` reports database connectivity and does not expose secrets.
- `npm run guardrails` before tests and build.
- `npm start` runs `prisma migrate deploy && next start`.
- Railway staging: `preDeployCommand` runs `npx prisma migrate deploy`, then `npx next start`, healthcheck `/api/health`, **exactly one replica**.
- `ALLOW_DEV_MAILBOX` is local/CI only and is ignored when `NODE_ENV=production`. `/api/dev/*` always 404s in production.
- Real email delivery uses the Resend HTTP API (`RESEND_API_KEY` + `EMAIL_FROM`). The API key is never placed in a URL.
- The development mailbox is used only when `NODE_ENV !== "production"` and `ALLOW_DEV_MAILBOX=true`. Production never falls back to it.
- `AUTH_URL` is the public origin for magic links, invitation URLs, and Auth.js redirects. Production redirects must never use `localhost` or `*.railway.internal`.
- Successful magic-link login without an invitation lands on authenticated home (`/`). Invitation callbacks stay on `/join/{token}` using the existing EMAIL/QR token model.
- Creating a table uses domain Blackjack defaults (`THREE_TWO` payout, 3 boxes, Insurance on). The creator is Bank/Dealer and remains in `TABLE_SETUP` until they start Blackjack or Poker.
- Home `CREATE TABLE` opens `/tables/new`, which creates or reuses one unused draft (`ensureDraftTable`) and redirects to `/tables/{id}` on the compact Create Table screen. Create Table invitations are inline in the PLAYERS section: exclusive Guest QR, Verified QR, and Email methods, no mask. `ClassicCreateTable` owns `selectedMethod` and passes it into `ClassicInviteMethods`, which mounts that method’s controls (Guest/Verified QR + Copy Link from existing join URLs/`joinQrDataUrl`, or email field + SEND INVITE via `inviteByEmail`). After `START TABLE`, Phase 0 uses one `ADD PLAYER` control that opens `ClassicInviteMask`. Guest QR (`/join/guest/{token}`, play name, table-scoped signed cookie, no email) and Verified QR (`/join/verified/{token}`, Auth.js magic link) are never shown together. Email invitations use the verified path. Add Local Player is an Owner-menu edge case. Guest users cannot create tables. Guest QR requires a connection to JetBro II Web; it is not offline/P2P.
- There are two reusable table QR join URLs with different intents. Multiple verified users may redeem the verified QR; each user gets one membership. Guest join is table-scoped and credits starting jetons once. Email send failures do not block QR or copy-link setup; the UI shows the configuration error.
- Join and membership changes bump `Table.updatedAt` so Owner/Dealer snapshots refresh. Blackjack `canStartBetting` is true when a Bank/Dealer is assigned and at least one active non-bank seated Player membership exists. Do not treat readiness as always true.
- During Phase 0 (`TABLE_SETUP` after `finalizeSetup`, or Poker `POKER_SETUP` while the Blackjack phase is still `TABLE_SETUP`) the Owner/Dealer screen shows compact Player positions, compact `Table setup` status, one `ADD PLAYER` control that opens the invitation mask, and `START BETTING` (`startBetting`) for Blackjack or `START HAND` (`startTexasHoldem`) for Poker. A seated Player sees `Waiting for the table to open betting.` Never show `Waiting for players` merely because one Player is present, and never show a waiting message while valid betting actions are available. A seated non-Dealer Player renders the Player Phase 0 board (`ClassicWaitingTable`), never the Dealer Phase 0 layout. `START BETTING` follows `canStartBetting`. `START HAND` follows `pokerControls()`. There is no giant empty Player placeholder. `START BLACKJACK` / `START POKER` are not shown on Create Table or Phase 0. Poker setup after switching from a live Blackjack table still uses the existing Poker Dealer `POKER_SETUP` screen.
- Screen choice is `selectTableBoard()` from snapshot flags only (`isDealer`, `isSeatedPlayer`, `isOwner`, game, phase). Dealer board stays primary when the viewer is both Dealer and a seated Player. Blackjack Phase 0 (`TABLE_SETUP` after setup is completed) uses the Owner/Dealer admin board when the viewer is Owner or Dealer, even if the Owner assigned the Bank to someone else; a seated non-Owner Player never receives that board. Roles are never inferred from name, email, or a leftover verified session. Table page, snapshot, stream, and command routes all pass the request `Cookie` header into `getActor`. On a table-scoped request, a matching guest cookie wins over Auth.js (`resolveActorFromIdentities`). Guest join sets `jetonbro.guest` and navigates with a full document load so the cookie is sent. `GET /api/tables/{id}/snapshot` is `Cache-Control: no-store`. Snapshots include `seatedPlayerCount` and `canStartBetting` so a same-ms join is not dropped. Table clients poll every 500ms and show an inline error when a command fails.
- Shared surfaces project the active game with `projectActiveGame`: Blackjack uses the Round phase; Poker uses the PokerHand phase. Home cards, table headers, SSE snapshot ordering, reconnect, save/close eligibility, and owner controls never show a stale Blackjack `Table.currentPhase` while Poker is active. Examples: `Texas Hold’em · PRE-FLOP`, `Texas Hold’em · SHOWDOWN`, `Texas Hold’em · HAND COMPLETE`. Closing or saving a Poker table is blocked while `LOCKED_POKER` exists or an active hand is unsettled.
- Next Poker hand: after `HAND_COMPLETE` the owner uses `NEXT HAND`. `NEXT HAND IN 7 SECONDS` stays in the table menu. The seven-second option stores `PokerHand.nextHandDeadlineAt`. Refresh resumes that deadline. At zero, or on `NEXT HAND`, the table rotates the dealer once, posts SB/BB once, and opens exactly one `PRE_FLOP` hand. Duplicate commands cannot create a second hand or post blinds twice.
- The current Poker actor’s seat uses a pulsing gold highlight (`prefers-reduced-motion` uses a static strong outline). Their screen says `YOUR TURN`; other screens say `TURN`. Every seat box shows name, AVAILABLE, current-street commitment, status (`YOUR TURN` / `TURN` / Waiting / FOLDED / ALL IN / WON), and D / SB / BB markers. The rotating Poker Dealer box has a D badge and a subtle gold border. The felt is identical for Owner and Players: centre pot is the jeton stack plus total of every committed hand contribution (`settled pots + current street contributions`), `TO CALL {amount}` only when the viewer owes on a live betting street, and main/side-pot lines only when side pots exist. After `HAND_COMPLETE` the pot area shows `POT PAID` and `{name} WON {amount}`; it never keeps `TO CALL`, an actor, or a Waiting seat. `TO CALL` and `CALL {amount}` use the same owed amount; `CALL 0` is never shown. A zero AVAILABLE stack does not receive Call/Bet/Raise and is marked All-In when that player is all-in. Optional Card Assist stays in Menu → Optional tools and does not appear on the default Poker felt. A player who cannot post a blind. Management controls stay out of the felt. Only that actor’s snapshot includes Fold/Check/Call/Bet/Raise/All-In. When chips are owed the actor sees CALL {amount} plus FOLD, RAISE and ALL IN. When nothing is owed they see CHECK, then BET if the street is unopened or RAISE if a wager already exists, plus ALL IN and FOLD. CHECK is never shown while `toCall > 0`. BET/RAISE opens one Classic numeric field; chips add to that field; CONFIRM commits once through `pokerAct`; CALL remains visible while composing a raise. Stale actions return `TURN_CONFLICT` and the client refreshes. Table Owner chrome (`isOwner`) is distinct from the rotating Dealer button (`seat.isDealer`). Owner street buttons `DEAL FLOP` / `DEAL TURN` / `DEAL RIVER` / `SHOWDOWN` sit in the phase-action area, compact and visually separated from actor actions, visible disabled with `Waiting for bets to match` until the street is complete, then enabled. Folded and All-In Players keep the wallet and seat status and receive no betting controls. Every playable Player screen uses a fixed bottom wallet (AVAILABLE on the right, shared jeton tray, safe-area padding) with game controls directly above it. The Poker table name appears once on the cloth (`data-table-name`), not in the header. Seat amounts are labelled AVAILABLE and STREET. ALL IN shows the stack. BET opens a street; RAISE uses a Raise-to composer with the legal minimum. A short all-in does not reopen raising for players who already acted. A fold-out awards the complete pot once, including the winner’s own committed blinds.
- During BETTING the Bank primary action is `DEAL CARDS` (`dealCards`). Secondary `ADD PLAYER` opens the existing invitation mask. `DEAL IN 7 SECONDS` remains a menu countdown. Both Deal actions require at least one valid locked player bet (`lockedBetMillis > 0`). Display leftover `originalStakeMillis` does not enable Deal. The seven-second option stores `Round.bettingCloseDeadlineAt` and closes betting exactly once at that deadline. Clients display the same countdown from that deadline. `DEAL CARDS` atomically clears that deadline and enters PLAYING exactly once. A repeated Deal while already PLAYING returns the current snapshot. A Deal sent from the wrong phase returns `PHASE_CONFLICT` and the client refreshes. Do not show the wording `CLOSE BETTING` in the normal game flow.
- Playing primary Bank action is `ENTER PAYOUT` (`enterPayout`). Show `OPEN INSURANCE` or `CLOSE INSURANCE`, never both. Payout primary action is `START BETTING` (`startNextRound`) after every box and required Insurance stake is settled. Do not show `START NEXT ROUND`.
- Visible Blackjack controls are derived from `src/ui/core/blackjack-phase-controls.ts`. Snapshot/engine labels may still say `CLOSE BETTING` / `START NEXT ROUND`; the Classic UI must not.
- Table stores `startingJetonsPerPlayerMillis`. When an invited user becomes a joined member, that membership is credited once (`starting-jetons:{tableId}:{userId}` plus `TableMember.startingJetonsCredited`). The Bank may later add more with the existing Bank-only control. The Bank is not a betting player.
- Redeem/join retries are idempotent: they do not create a second membership or credit starting jetons twice.
- Betting commands return domain errors (`INSUFFICIENT_FUNDS`, phase/permission messages). A joined Player with starting jetons can lock AVAILABLE into LOCKED_BET during BETTING.
- Live table snapshots use in-process SSE with a short snapshot poll fallback. The listener set is stored on `globalThis` so Next.js module duplication cannot drop updates. Each snapshot includes a server `revision` (`Table.updatedAt` from the database, never client time) and `roundNumber`. Clients and SSE ignore any older in-flight snapshot so a successful Deal cannot be overwritten by a stale BETTING payload. Command failures refresh the snapshot. `Table.currentPhase` is repaired to match `Round.phase` when they diverge. If `currentPhase` is BETTING with no current round, `START BETTING` (`startBetting`) creates the missing BETTING round. Snapshot and SSE loads skip Blackjack close-betting and next-round timers while `Table.game` is not `BLACKJACK`, including the race immediately after switching to Texas Hold’em. Phase commands log sanitized evidence (table, round, actor, requested transition, phase, round status, bet counts, unresolved counts, deadlines, result code) and never log emails, tokens, join links, or secrets.

## JETBRO II MVP FINALISATION MODE

Before working:

1. Read `docs/MVP_FILE_MAP.md`.
2. Read `docs/DESIGN_AUTHORITY.md`.
3. Identify one role/phase slice.
4. Open mapped files for that slice first.
5. For a specifically authorised route/component/CSS audit, Cursor may inspect all UI routes, render selectors, Classic components and imported stylesheets. It may remove proven-dead visual routes, components and selectors. It must not alter domain, accounting, authentication or command behaviour. File-count limits do not apply to an authorised consolidation pass, but every changed production file must be justified.

During work:

- Preserve frozen engine files.
- No opportunistic domain refactoring.
- No test-library regeneration.
- Do not expand gameplay swipe gestures, Card Assist, timers or Zilch. Owner swipe-left on a Home saved-table card is permitted as a visual shortcut when the same action remains available through an accessible menu. Blackjack payout swipe behaviour remains unchanged.
- One visual/functional slice at a time unless this prompt authorises a consolidation pass.

Testing:

- Visual-only work: guardrails, affected component tests, affected responsive Playwright/screenshots and production build.
- Accounting, authentication, identity, phase-machine, migration or release work: full acceptance process.
- Do not run the historical full Playwright catalogue for isolated visual changes unless specifically requested or the focused tests reveal a cross-cutting regression.

## Change discipline

From here, implementation requests use lightweight prompts unless the work falls under the full acceptance process.

Keep the existing architecture, domain rules, ledger, auth, and Classic skin boundaries intact. Implement only the requested change. Protocol, accounting, and phase-machine work must not include a visual redesign.

### Lightweight prompts (default)

Read this file first.

Implement only the requested change. Keep the existing architecture, domain rules, ledger, auth and Classic skin boundaries intact.

Visual-only work: guardrails, affected component tests, affected responsive Playwright/screenshots and production build.

Accounting, authentication, identity, phase-machine, migration or release work: full acceptance process.

Do not run the historical full Playwright catalogue for isolated visual changes unless specifically requested or the focused tests reveal a cross-cutting regression.

Do not run the full Playwright suite, generate screenshots, update architecture documents, commit, push or deploy unless explicitly requested.

For visual, copy, or layout changes, affected tests plus build are sufficient until several improvements are batched into one deployment. Make small changes locally, leave them for review, and deploy only when a batch is accepted.

Do not claim completion from code inspection alone.

### Full acceptance process

Use the full acceptance process only for:

- Accounting or ledger changes
- Authentication / invitations
- Phase transitions
- Database migrations
- Releases to Railway

Full acceptance means:

1. Read this file.
2. Read the files and tests directly affected.
3. State the existing invariant or behavior being changed.
4. Keep the change within one vertical slice.
5. Run focused tests during development.
6. Run guardrails, the full Vitest suite, production build, and the Playwright coverage that proves the changed flow.
7. Render affected 390x844 mobile states and verify at 320x700 when the UI is part of the change.
8. Update this file and `CHANGELOG.md` when architectural facts, invariants, permissions, commands, deployment, or status changed.
9. Commit, push, and deploy only when explicitly requested.
10. Report exact results and genuine limitations.

## Current implementation line

- Repository: JetBro II
- Default skin: Tabletop (`src/ui/skins/tabletop/`); Classic is the registered rollback skin
- Games: Blackjack and Texas Hold’em
- Active visual authority: original approved PNGs in `design/reference/classic/approved/` (literal anatomy). Product contracts control commands/roles/data. HTML prototype is secondary token reference only.
- Next agreed milestone: polish Tabletop visual fidelity against approved PNG crops (spacing/density/type) while freezing engine/accounting; Home/Create Table remain functional on the same token system
- Classic CSS isolation retained: active Tabletop bundle must not load Classic stylesheets (`registry` → `classic/skin`)
- Tabletop presentation primitives live under `src/ui/skins/tabletop/components/primitives/`; Blackjack Dealer uses dense ledger rows; Player uses `PlayerBox` + `JetonTray`; structural `TableRail` SVG on Shell felt
- Zilch: deferred
- Release/deployment status belongs in `CHANGELOG.md` and `docs/IMPLEMENTATION_LOG.md`, not this rules file.
